course: dictionary
lesson: 12486
title: Reading how people behave
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A demeanour is the way a person looks and behaves, and it shows their mood or character. You cannot see what someone feels inside, but you can often see it in their demeanour.
explain: Writers use demeanour to show what a character is like without saying it directly. «Mrs Patel had a calm demeanour, so the nervous children felt safe.» Calm tells you how she acts: she is quiet, steady and relaxed.
explain: Look for clue words around demeanour, such as calm, cheerful, nervous or cold. Ask yourself: how is this person acting, and what does that show about how they feel?
fact: Demeanour is a noun. It names a way of looking and behaving.
fact: «Demeanour» means the way someone looks and behaves, which shows their mood or character.
fact: Words often used with demeanour include calm, friendly, nervous, cheerful and cold.
fact: Useful phrases: «a calm demeanour», «a friendly demeanour», «a change of demeanour».
fact: In American English the word is spelled demeanor, without the u.
exercise: «Mrs Patel spoke to the class with a calm demeanour.» What does demeanour mean here? | The homework she set | *The way she looked and behaved | The room where she taught | The noise the class made
exercise: «When the bell rang, Tom's cheerful demeanour changed to a gloomy one.» What does change of demeanour show? | Tom lost his bag | Tom's coat was wet | The bell was broken | *Tom's mood changed
exercise: Which word could describe a demeanour that makes people feel safe? | *Calm | Muddy | Ancient | Barely
test: «The new girl kept a shy demeanour all week.» What does shy suggest about her? | She had forgotten her lunch | *She was quiet and unsure around others | She was brilliant at maths | She was loud and bossy
test: «The guard's cold demeanour made the visitors nervous.» What does cold demeanour suggest? | *The guard looked and acted unfriendly | The guard was cold because it was winter | The guard was asleep | The guard had lost his keys
exam: «The new girl kept a shy demeanour all week, until she laughed at Sam's joke on Friday.» What does this show about her demeanour? | It was loud and bossy from the start | It had nothing to do with her mood | *It changed, because she became more relaxed and friendly | It stayed exactly the same all week
